@@ -65,3 +65,11 @@ These hold for every record, however it was made.
 - Fridges must read at or below 5 °C and freezers at or below -15 °C. Each
   of them needs at least one reading per day.
 - Allergens are the 14 EU allergens, stored lowercase and sorted.
+
+## Sites (schema 3)
+
+The `sites` list contains site ids and names. Every location has a `site`
+referencing that list; batches and stock-takes belong to a site through their
+location. Schema 2 migrates to a single `main` site with all existing locations;
+schema 1 first migrates to schema 2. Migration preserves stock and history.
+Items, suppliers, recipes and dishes are shared across sites.
